{"title":"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Kiran Kedlaya</i>) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime number and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd179d1168fa2c69e93a029d3991ac3c937dd4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; s &lt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that there exist integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d24cbc1fc966a351497c8807b36e95b1bc4340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; m &lt; n &lt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" /> and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11aa6702c8ca4b94cb3a0fa3c2e33b161aab817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ \\frac{sm}{p} \\right\\} &lt; \\left\\{ \\frac{sn}{p} \\right\\} &lt; \\frac{s}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"165\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Note: For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> a real number, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denote the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fc6a0d316131539a685aca6deee35129c1dc93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\} = x - \\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> denote the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We proceed by contradiction.  Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4485880ad6eced5d6a062bf481d332ada73dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s|(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.  Then for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13eb714de44ef290ccc2992c03b70e285bf67816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sk=p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />.  The conditions given are equivalent to stating that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebacb3cf1326c851b830774313abef131af5da28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sm \\bmod p &lt; sn \\bmod p&lt; s\\bmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" />.\nNow consider the following array modulo p:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d5f7d96ea22fc6f05266065e788b91f600ed6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{ccccc} \\mbox{Row 1}&amp; s&amp; 2s&amp;\\hdots&amp; ks\\\\ \\mbox{Row 2}&amp; s-1&amp; 2s-1&amp; \\hdots&amp;ks-1\\\\ \\vdots&amp;\\vdots&amp;\\vdots&amp;\\ddots&amp;\\vdots\\\\ \\mbox{Row }s&amp; 1&amp; s+1&amp; \\hdots&amp; (k-1)s+1 \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"90\" />\n</p><p>Obviously, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> columns. The first entry of each row is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c4909098265979cd9f6e9b7f193e1812a5d0b82c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((r-1)k+1)s\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />.  Since we wish for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8963aea7342ad65db9da1ff8ecf8bc497dad37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sm\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b390d1257225244793a6d203cf0f93445ef4f280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sn\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> to both be in the first column, while also satisfying the given conditions, we can easily see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce586d3c35ad6966105bed9d053009164982c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sm$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> must be in a row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475ae07f7fd5eb82d386c484b3ddc3bc549c0f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6dfabb5193247b9e1958ee01237dc85e1072a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_r&gt;n_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2611b9515ac58ccc6ffb6710fa9162266f243703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> denotes the row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e0fd626789d74e2d14522219b8862bef819ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sn \\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> is in.  However, since the values of each entry decreases while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af9d24bfab49ca422189e050381dc5d598fbd4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((r-1)k+1)s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> keeps increasing, we can see that the condition can never be satisfied and thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f2d5dea78000505f147592699a495a6aadf9b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\not|(p-1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>To prove the other direction, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1308ec1fe23cb44a1fd165547ed93affc8c88f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sj+r=p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> being the largest integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9620178183bd4b6f89412134924fed1617f47a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sj&lt;p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f843e1e94d31381883702866a95e8bf6d27d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&lt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc45fb4599dd3ed28d925ded4b20fc2bcb4a4d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\not|(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018efa9906a486810d92d26de9f5bcde232584f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;s&lt;p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3232ecd4507c5638a1cd5ab356717ea18edb1cff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;l&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d72170f503456a0208d4115f9ce491a466fcdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ls\\ge s\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />.  Thus, the first integer multiplied by s modulo p that will be less than s is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98895b0c81ceb090bdf70971056591667b0344a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j+1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/9329109a5f91b535757f8d3c75edfa9385ab7f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j+1)s\\equiv s-r-1\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafcfe418c3c803aa52c5047c77378fe931f145b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lbrace s,2s,\\hdots,js,(j+1)s,\\hdots,xs,\\hdots,(p-1)s \\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" /> is a complete residue system mod p with the exception of the 0 term, we can find an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8504f517f1c35b0b97c5261082c156e6e535a41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;j+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19b7724e235e3203c778c31279174a0122522ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xs \\equiv s-1 \\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/719f75f7e9d8c6ee7eee9715876e6018e30b2df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=j+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80449fafe8a8369f8f3c43d8a206459a70a3b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"10\" /> to complete the proof.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=84548 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO\" title=\"2006 USAMO\">2006 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017060949\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1634/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8880/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.036      1 -total\n 42.20%    7.612      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 29.51%    5.323      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 26.79%    4.831      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3183:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017060949 and revision id 194697. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}